<title>UK: Brown not extending VAT to food, kid's clothes.</title>
<headline>Brown not extending VAT to food, kid's clothes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown said on Wednesday that he would not be extending the scope of value added-tax (VAT) to cover books, newspapers, children's clothes, food and public transport. He said he would not extend VAT to the above, exempt areas in this budget. &quot;Nor will I during this parliament,&quot; he said in his budget speech.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
